5. The Root–Defiled Triad 1197

Dependent on a root-state that is undefiled-but-defilable, a root-state that is undefiled-but-defilable arises, by root condition: three.

Dependent on a root-state that is undefiled-but-defilable and a non-root-state that is undefiled-but-defilable, a root-state that is undefiled-but-defilable arises, by root condition: three. By root condition: nine; by object condition: nine; by predominance condition: nine; by non-disappearance condition: nine.

Dependent on a non-root-state that is undefiled-but-defilable, a non-root-state that is undefiled-but-defilable arises —
not by root condition: one;
not by object condition: three;
not by predominance condition: nine;
not by proximity condition: three;
not by contiguity condition: three;
not by mutuality condition: three;
not by decisive-support condition: three;
not by prenascence condition: nine;
not by postnascence condition: nine;
not by repetition condition: nine;
not by kamma condition: three;
not by result condition: nine;
not by nutriment condition: one;
not by faculty condition: one;
not by jhāna condition: one;
not by path condition: one;
not by association condition: three;
not by dissociation condition: nine;
not by absence condition: three;
not by disappearance condition: three.

By root condition, by object condition: three. Not by root condition, by object condition: one.

(In the Conascence Section too, in the Condition Section too, in the Support Section too, in the Conjunction Section too, in the Association Section too — the elaboration is to be understood as similar to the Dependence Section.)

A root-state that is undefiled-but-defilable is a condition, by root condition, for a root-state that is undefiled-but-defilable: three.

A root-state that is undefiled-but-defilable is a condition, by object condition, for a root-state that is undefiled-but-defilable: nine.

A root-state that is undefiled-but-defilable is a condition, by predominance condition — as object-predominance, as conascence-predominance — for a root-state that is undefiled-but-defilable: three.

A non-root-state that is undefiled-but-defilable is a condition, by predominance condition — as object-predominance, as conascence-predominance — for a non-root-state that is undefiled-but-defilable: three.

A root-state that is undefiled-but-defilable, together with a non-root-state that is undefiled-but-defilable, is a condition, by predominance condition — as object-predominance — for a root-state that is undefiled-but-defilable: three.

