**20. Hetu-Sārammaṇa Duka-tika** 1235

Object-predominance, co-nascent-predominance: three.

A non-root phenomenon having an object is a condition for a non-root phenomenon having an object, by way of the predominance condition — object-predominance, co-nascent-predominance: three.

Both a root phenomenon having an object and a non-root phenomenon having an object are a condition for a root phenomenon having an object, by way of the predominance condition — object-predominance: three.

By way of the root condition: three. By way of the object condition: nine. By way of the predominance condition: nine. By way of the immediacy condition: nine. By way of the contiguity condition: nine. By way of the co-nascence condition: nine. By way of the mutuality condition: nine. By way of the support condition: nine. By way of the decisive-support condition: nine. By way of the repetition condition: nine. By way of the kamma condition: three. By way of the result condition: nine. By way of the nutriment condition: three. By way of the faculty condition: nine. By way of the non-disappearance condition: nine.

A root phenomenon having an object is a condition for a root phenomenon having an object, by way of the object condition, by way of the co-nascence condition, by way of the decisive-support condition. Not by way of the root condition: nine. Not by way of the object condition: nine. [It is a condition,] not by way of the root condition, [but] by way of the object condition: three. Not by way of the root condition, nor by way of the object condition: nine.

(As was reckoned for the forward order, the forward-order of conditions, and the forward-order-of-conditions in the Wholesome section on wisdom, so should this be reckoned.)

The Hetu-Sārammaṇa duka-tika is concluded.

**20. Hetu-Sārammaṇa Duka-tika** [continued — dependence section]

Depending on a root phenomenon having an object, a root phenomenon having an object arises, by way of the root condition: three.

Depending on a non-root phenomenon having an object, a non-root phenomenon having an object arises, by way of the root condition: three.

Depending on both a root phenomenon having an object and a non-root phenomenon having an object, a root phenomenon having an object arises, by way of the root condition: three.

By way of the root condition: nine. By way of the object condition: nine. By way of the predominance condition: nine. By way of the kamma condition: nine. By way of the result condition: nine. By way of the nutriment condition: nine. By way of the non-disappearance condition: nine.

Depending on a non-root phenomenon having an object, a non-root phenomenon having an object arises — [but] not by way of the root condition.

Depending on a root phenomenon having an object, a root phenomenon having an object arises — not by way of the root condition.

Depending on a root phenomenon having an object, a non-root phenomenon having an object arises — not by way of the object condition.

Depending on a non-root phenomenon having an object, a root phenomenon having an object arises — not by way of the object condition.

Depending on both a root phenomenon having an object and a non-root phenomenon having an object, a non-root phenomenon having an object arises — not by way of the object condition.

Depending on a non-root phenomenon having an object, a root phenomenon having an object arises — not by way of the predominance condition:

