**11. Paccanīya Dukatika Paṭṭhāna 1481**

Dependent on a non-wholesome dhamma that is non-visible and impinging, a non-wholesome dhamma that is non-visible and impinging arises by condition of root;
dependent on a non-wholesome dhamma that is non-visible and impinging, a non-unwholesome dhamma that is non-visible and impinging arises by condition of root;
dependent on a non-wholesome dhamma that is non-visible and impinging, both a non-wholesome and a non-unwholesome dhamma, non-visible and impinging, arise together by condition of root.
By root: twenty-nine. On obtaining: twenty-nine. (All should be understood in full.)

Dependent on a non-wholesome dhamma that is invisible and impinging, a non-wholesome dhamma that is invisible and impinging arises by condition of root. By root: twenty-nine. On obtaining: twenty-nine. (All should be understood in full.)

Dependent on a non-wholesome dhamma that is invisible and non-impinging, a non-wholesome dhamma that is invisible and non-impinging arises by condition of root. By root: nine. (All should be understood in full.)

